<article class="env-lemma" id="06PE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06PE">Lemma <span data-tag="06PE">78.27.1</span>.</a> Notation and assumption as in Lemma <a href="/tag/046Q" data-tag="046Q">78.21.1</a>. The morphism of quotient stacks </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [f] : [U/R] \longrightarrow [U'/R']  \]
</div>
  <p> turns $[U/R]$ into a gerbe over $[U'/R']$ if $f : U \to U'$ and $R \to R'|_ U$ are surjective maps of fppf sheaves. Here $R'|_ U$ is the restriction of $R'$ to $U$ via $f : U \to U'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will verify that Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/06P1" data-tag="06P1">8.11.3</a> properties (2) (a) and (2) (b) hold. Property (2)(a) holds because $U \to U'$ is a surjective map of sheaves (use Lemma <a href="/tag/044X" data-tag="044X">78.24.1</a> to see that objects in $[U'/R']$ locally come from $U'$). To prove (2)(b) let $x, y$ be objects of $[U/R]$ over a scheme $T/S$. Let $x', y'$ be the images of $x, y$ in the category $[U'/'R]_ T$. Condition (2)(b) requires us to check the map of sheaves 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathit{Isom}(x, y) \longrightarrow \mathit{Isom}(x', y')  \]
</div>
    <p>
       on $(\mathit{Sch}/T)_{fppf}$ is surjective. To see this we may work fppf locally on $T$ and assume that come from $a, b \in U(T)$. In that case we see that $x', y'$ correspond to $f \circ a, f \circ b$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/044V" data-tag="044V">78.22.1</a> the displayed map of sheaves in this case becomes 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T \times _{(a, b), U \times _ B U} R \longrightarrow T \times _{f \circ a, f \circ b, U' \times _ B U'} R' = T \times _{(a, b), U \times _ B U} R'|_ U.  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence the assumption that $R \to R'|_ U$ is a surjective map of fppf sheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ implies the desired surjectivity. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>